{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01W7DGUZrMJJpk2BmQfzzc8W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's an experiment in specification-driven code generation using mage-claude-orchestrator.\n\n**Architecture**: Specifications in `docs/specs/` drive code generation into `cmd/<name>/` (one binary per utility) and `pkg/` (shared libraries: sys, format, testutils, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil). Verification is byte-for-byte comparison against GNU reference binaries via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`.\n\n**Current state**: Generation run 44 is in progress. Many utilities are implemented across releases 00.0–09.1. The most recent commit completed cmd/truncate (srd083 R3.1–R3.3). The requirement_states field shows all remaining ready requirements.\n\n**Priority release**: The earliest release with ready requirements is **rel10.1** — permission and ownership utilities (chmod, chgrp, chown). All 13 chmod requirements, 10 chgrp requirements, and 10 chown requirements are in \"ready\" state.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nFocusing on **srd089-chmod** (rel10.1). With 13 requirements and a 4-task limit, all 4 tasks go to chmod implementation. chgrp and chown are deferred to the next batch. Tests are deferred per P2 (split implementation and tests).\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight 1 per requirement (requirements.yaml weights not provided in project_context):\n\n- Task 0: srd089 R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1) → total 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: srd089 R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1) → total 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: srd089 R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1) → total 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: srd089 R4.1 (w=1), R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1) → total 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/chmod core mode parsing and applicat